  "interpretation": "<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99%; border-width: 1px; border-spacing: 0px;\" border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" data-cke-table-faked-selection-table=\"\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><strong>Log IU/mL</strong></span></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><strong>Result In IU/ml</strong></span></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><strong>Remarks</strong></span></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><strong>Conclusion</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;&lt;2</span></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;&lt; 100</span></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Indicates absence of HIV-2 RNA or it is present</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">below the detection limit of the assy</span></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Negative</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;&gt;2</span></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;&gt;100</span></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Indicates presence of HIV-2 RNA</span></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Positive</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Intermediate</span></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\">&nbsp;</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Inhibitors detected in sample provided</span></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Repeat testing of fresh sample is</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">recommended</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><strong>**Linear reporting &nbsp;range of this assay &nbsp;is 50 IU/ml to 50 x 109 IU/ml (2.17-10.17 log IU/ml).</strong></span><br><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><strong>Note</strong></span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">1.&nbsp;Positive result indicates the presence of HIV2 RNA in the given sample obtained by targeting the Long Terminal Repeat (LTR) region of the HIV-2 genome.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">2.&nbsp;(HIV-2) infections present unique challenges due to low viral titers, slow disease progression, and poor response to standard antiviral therapies.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">3.&nbsp;Negative result indicates the absence of HIV-2 RNA in the given sample.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">4.&nbsp;False-negative results may occur due to , low viral load below the detectable limit in the specimen, potential mutation in target region of HIV 2 RNA covered by the primers &amp; probe used in the kit and presence of inhibitor may result in under quantification / failure to detect pathogen in given sample.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">5. Results should be used to aid in the diagnosis of HIV2 &nbsp;infection and must be interpreted in the context of host risk factors and clinical presentation.</span></p>",
